## How to use it

1. Settle the rows marked "Settle" and update the Expected column.
2. When the classifier and the guardrails are built, run every query through the App and record what it did.
3. Build a table of expected vs. actual, and count how often each label is confused with another. A single accuracy number hides which kind of mistake is happening.
4. Decide in advance which mistakes cost the most. A wrongly declined follow-up (23 or 25) or a verdict given on rows 21, 22 and 35 is worse than a factual question labeled ambiguous.
5. Keep this file in the repo. The set, the confusion table and the accuracy bar you chose are case-study evidence.